{
  "arguments": {
    "query": "vLLM prefix caching block hash parent hash token IDs extra hash"
  },
  "observation": {
    "evidence": [
      {
        "id": "E722fbbcc372bd4a54fbb26a3",
        "chunk_id": "ba41f1809d2ccb3fb1e3ecbb",
        "parent_id": "3094435fb062ce4a1b5f4dd4",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L47-L77",
        "content": "```text\nBlock 0\n    Parent hash: None\n    Token IDs: 1, 3, 7493, 1681, 1294, 1593, 3937, 9551, <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 1\n    Parent hash: Block 0 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 2\n    Parent hash: Block 1 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 3\n    Parent hash: Block 2 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>, 4\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\n```",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E5cd53a2e3cb929c22be31ed5",
        "chunk_id": "a3e5c4e7c85d6b5597e79aa6",
        "parent_id": "2cea061deb042236c244b028",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L15-L19",
        "content": "* Parent hash value: The hash value of the parent hash block.\n* Block tokens: A tuple of tokens in this block.\nThe reason to include the exact tokens is to reduce potential hash value collision.\n* Extra hashes: Other values required to make this block unique, such as LoRA IDs, multi-modality input hashes (see the example below), and cache salts to isolate caches in multi-tenant environments.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Ea15ac575d0077997740e8e1e",
        "chunk_id": "831e35484dd2ca27088ebde3",
        "parent_id": "49360f163824e6436d30ab06",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L24-L29",
        "content": "!!\n! note \"Note 2\"\nThe above hash key structure is not 100% collision free.\nTheoretically it’s still possible for the different prefix tokens to have the same hash value.\nTo avoid any hash collisions **in a multi-tenant setup, we advise to use SHA256** as hash function instead of the default builtin hash.\nSHA256 is supported since vLLM v0.8.3 and must be enabled with a command line argument.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E881a6028445aaeece4403f8c",
        "chunk_id": "a756e1212e535b1d75e47a3f",
        "parent_id": "5e18fdc07bd0b1d756518f71",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L178-L192",
        "content": "In v0, when detecting block 3 is duplicated, we free block 3 and let Request 2 use block 1 instead, so its block table becomes `[0, 1]` in Time 1.\nHowever, the block table in vLLM v1 is append-only, meaning that changing the block table from `[0, 3]` to `[0, 1]` is not allowed.\nAs a result, we will have duplicated blocks for the hash key E-H.\nThis duplication will be eliminated when the request is freed.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E620d3ddaad5ad2054c752d19",
        "chunk_id": "779175155be2b4c482fd5c25",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "To improve privacy in shared environments, vLLM supports isolating prefix cache reuse through optional per-request salting.\nBy including a `cache_salt` in the request, this value is injected into the hash of the first block, ensuring that only requests with the same salt can reuse cached KV blocks.\nThis prevents timing-based attacks where an adversary could infer cached content by observing latency differences.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E4881760a03b3e8acc341bd12",
        "chunk_id": "e0102b010d94e4bdb7f68e26",
        "parent_id": "3094435fb062ce4a1b5f4dd4",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L47-L77",
        "content": "The challenge for prefix caching to support this case is we need to differentiate images from the placeholders.\nTo address this problem, we encode the image hash generated by the frontend image processor.\nFor example, the hash of the blocks in the above prompt would be (assuming block size 16, and we have 41 placeholder tokens):",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Eb84bdda9ff6e6568d86f5bd3",
        "chunk_id": "95411643ef936e459d8993e9",
        "parent_id": "2cea061deb042236c244b028",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L15-L19",
        "content": "In the example above, the KV cache in the first block can be uniquely identified with the token “A gentle breeze stirred”.\nThe third block can be uniquely identified with the tokens in the block “laughed in the distance”, along with the prefix tokens “A gentle breeze stirred the leaves as children”.\nTherefore, we can build the block hash of `hash(tuple[components])`, where components are:",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E1c5b7341c4d64d891d9a1cfe",
        "chunk_id": "7c1a6df7e7a23c7671ff1794",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "!!\n! note\nCache isolation is not supported in engine V0.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
